.TH VIOLA-LANDLORD 6 "2026" "viola-landlord @VERSION@" "Games"
.SH NAME
viola-landlord \- The Landlord's Game (Lizzie J. Magie, 1904) against the computer, for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viola-landlord
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.br
.B viola\-landlord \-\-relay
.I port
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Viola the Landlord
plays
.IR "The Landlord's Game" ,
the board game patented by Lizzie J. Magie in 1904 (US Patent 748,626)
and the ancestor of Monopoly, by the rules published by the Economic Game
Company of New York in 1906, including the
.B Single Tax
rules. Two to four players sit at the table: each seat is a human at this
screen (players take turns at the keyboard) or a computer player at an
.BR Easy ,
.B Medium
or
.B Hard
level. Players on other machines can join over
.BR ssh (1);
see NETWORK PLAY. The window is drawn in the style of the Viola web browser: flat
gray94 panels, raised bevels, black focus boxes, Helvetica menus.
.PP
The game ends when a player has drawn his wages five times (three, seven or
ten can be chosen); the richest player wins, counting cash and 100 for each
card, house and luxury.
.SH PLAYING
On your turn press
.B Roll Dice
(Space or Enter). Whenever the rules give you a choice \(em buying a lot,
bidding, paying the jail fine, using a railroad pass, moving backward
between the Chances, speculating, buying a luxury \(em a dialog asks.
Before rolling you may build houses, buy or sell cards, or propose the
Single Tax from the
.B Game
menu. Click a space on the board to read about it.
.SH NETWORK PLAY
One player chooses
.BR "Game > Host a Network Game" ;
up to three others choose
.B "Game > Join a Network Game"
and give the host's machine as
.B ssh
would,
.RI [ user\fB@\fP] host [\fB:\fP port ].
The joiner's game runs
.PP
.RS
.B ssh \-T \-o BatchMode=yes
.I user\fB@\fPhost
.B viola\-landlord \-\-relay
.I port
.RE
.PP
and the relay connects to the hosting game, which listens on 127.0.0.1 only
(port 1904 unless the host chose another). Four players at most: a fifth is
turned away with a warning. When fewer than four humans play, one computer
player takes a free seat; with four humans there is none. A joiner whose
connection drops is replaced by a computer player.
.PP
Password-less ssh (a key, e.g.
.B ssh\-keygen
then
.BR ssh\-copy\-id )
is required; check it with
.BR "ssh \-o BatchMode=yes user@host viola\-landlord \-\-version" .
.TP
.BI \-\-relay " port"
(run by ssh on the host, not by hand) connect standard input and output to
the game hosted on this machine.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Space ", " Enter ", " R
roll the dice
.TP
.B B
build a house
.TP
.BR T " / " S
buy a card from, or sell a card to, a computer player
.TP
.B X
propose the Single Tax
.TP
.B F1
how to play
.TP
.B F2
the standings
.TP
.BR PgUp " / " PgDn " / " End
scroll the record of events
.TP
.BR Esc ", " F9 ", " F10
the menu bar; Alt+G, Alt+O, Alt+H open a menu
.TP
.BR Ctrl+N " / " Ctrl+Q
new game / quit
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/viola-landlord/preferences.conf
(normally
.IR ~/.config/viola-landlord/preferences.conf )
the seats
.RI ( seat1 " .. " seat4 :
empty, human, easy, medium, hard), the human players' names
.RI ( name1 " .. " name4 ),
the length of the game, the rules, the options, and for network play
.IR net_host ,
.IR net_port ,
.I net_command
(the program ssh runs on the host; give a full path if it is not on the
host's PATH for non-interactive ssh) and
.IR net_cpu ,
as
.I key = value
lines.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
the X display to use.
.SH NOTES
The board is drawn after the layout of Magie's 1904 patent drawing; the
rules are those of the patent and of 1906. Both are in the public domain.
All pictures are original to this program. The exact order of some spaces,
the land rent of each lot and the Chance cards are not given by the
surviving 1906 rule text and are reconstructed; see README.md.
.SH AUTHOR
Lee Curtis.
